flowchart TB
accTitle: Reusing a frozen tokenizer during training and inference
accDescr: Prepared training text and application input converge on the same configured tokenizer. Application input first undergoes extraction or message formatting when required. The frozen tokenizer normalizes, pre-tokenizes and applies learned rules to produce token IDs. IDs become training sequences and masks, or inference input. Corpus-wide filtering and deduplication are not repeated for every prompt.
 A["Prepared LLM-training text"] --> C["Model-specific input format<br/>Document or message boundaries"]
 B["User text, files, messages"] --> P["Application processing as needed<br/>Extraction and chat / tool serialization"]
 C --> N["Configured normalization<br/>May be identity"]
 P --> N
 N --> Q["Configured pre-tokenization<br/>Then apply learned vocabulary and rules"]
 T["Frozen tokenizer artifact"] -. "Same version and text rules" .-> Q
 Q --> I["Token IDs"]
 I --> L["LLM training<br/>Sequences, packing, attention / loss masks"]
 I --> R["Inference<br/>Context and batching; model execution"]
 class A,B source;
 class C,P corpus;
 class T learning;
 class N,Q encoding;
 class I,L,R output;

classDef source fill:#edf1f5,stroke:#8495a5,color:#202b38;
